  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Beyon the SetSyncType, mentioned here: https://feedback.vrchat.com/sdk-bug-reports/p/vrcsyncvideostreamsetsynctype-is-broken\nThere seem to be issues with general Play RPC and late joiner syncing.\nI shoved 4 different accounts into one instance and each one was getting different results.\nThe world is set up to have autoplay (doesnt work) and have a Play OnNetworkReady RPC (doesnt do anything either).\nClicking Next makes the videos play on the master and for the players that are present in the room.\nLate Joiners: this is where it becomes very random.\nWhen a late joiner joins they get either of the scenarios:\n- They see the player playing (usually for the first late joiner not long after master)\n- They see the player stutter as it is getting paused and unpaused all the time. Resyncing, changing max resolution, calling Play RPC on the Owner doesnt fix it. Only fix is to call Stop and Play RPCs.\n- They see the player stopped. Only way to play is to call Stop + Play or Next RPCs.\nCombined with the fact that master triggers are clickable by everyone right now - this makes the player pretty unusable for any kind of live event. So far I had to click stop+play for every late joiner to see the player playing 90% of the time, which results in horrible experience for everyone in the lobby.\nWorld to test: https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_64143376-95bc-469a-ae77-0626c4d85be0\nOn the far left speaker column in the main area of the world - click on \"Dvize\" in the DJ list. This will turn on Monstercat stream that goes 24/7\nExample of a late joiner experience (note that Stop and Play supposed to be Master Only): https://streamable.com/2zgu4w\nThis is on latest SDK.",
